Notebook[{Cell["K14n12345: a Wolfram computation", "Title"], 
  Cell["From a triangulation signature to hyperbolic volume and a candidate \
Dirichlet domain", "Subtitle"], Cell["All geometry is computed in Wolfram \
Language. The public SnapPy dataset supplies combinatorial input only; no \
SnapPy, SnapPea, Regina, or Python runtime is called.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Volume = 18.3653611016104753434064495431359322443623576", "Text"], 
  Cell["Drag each graphic to rotate. Orange points are ideal vertices; the \
center point is the chosen Dirichlet basepoint. There are 84 faces. Both \
models depict the same hyperbolic polyhedron.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Poincare ball", "Section"], 
